-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt — a little light experiment
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s original C++ smallpt path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly and presented as an interactive browser experiment.
 
+## Run
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install
+pnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+Open `/`. The home page is also prerendered to `dist/client/index.html` during production builds. Serve the output over HTTP; Web Workers and WebAssembly do not load from `file://`.
 
-## Tech Stack
+The page renders automatically. **Randomize & render** changes the two walls and both sphere colors and restarts the renderer. Samples and resolution controls rerender the current palette. **Save image** downloads the current canvas as a PNG.
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+## Build
+
+```sh
+pnpm build
+pnpm start
+```
+
+The compiled `.wasm` and its ES module loader are checked in, so Emscripten is only needed when changing the C++ source:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build:wasm
+pnpm check:wasm
+```
+
+`build:wasm` requires `em++` (tested with Emscripten 6.0.1). The check executes the shipped WebAssembly in a Node VM with a Worker-like environment; it checks progressive RGBA output, sphere recoloring, and repeatable seeded rendering, without launching a browser.
+
+## Implementation
+
+- `native/smallpt-original.cpp`: unmodified original smallpt source.
+- `native/smallpt-web.cpp`: browser adapter preserving the original Monte Carlo integrator, 2×2 subpixel sampling, reflection and refraction. Accumulates independent passes and exposes RGBA pixels instead of writing a PPM.
+- `public/wasm/render-worker.js`: runs all tracing in a dedicated module worker and transfers progressive frames to the main thread. Restarting terminates the previous worker.
+- `src/scripts/smallpt.ts`: canvas, palette, quality controls, progress and PNG export.
+- `public/images/smallpt-reference.png`: Kevin Beason’s reference render from the original distribution, displayed while the first client-side frame is computed.
+
+Single-worker execution requires no cross-origin isolation headers. Rendering uses the visitor’s CPU, with no rendering service or uploaded data.
+
+Original source and reference image: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/ . Copyright © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason, MIT license; preserved in `native/LICENSE.txt` and `public/wasm/LICENSE.txt`.
